  "body": "Allow the AI chat panel to host user-installed external ACP coding agents over an authenticated local MCP bridge.\n\n## Scope\n- Add an opt-in per-session auth token option to `Inbox::listen` (`--mcp-port` in `crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs`) and `camcraft-cli mcp --connect` (`crates/app/src/mcp/bridge.rs`).\n- Add an ACP `ChatBackend` implementation under `#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]` to launch user-installed CLI agents (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`) over stdio JSON-RPC with cancel (`session/cancel`) and MCP bridge configuration.\n- Keep this launcher optional after Slice 1 so users without external CLIs use the built-in HTTP provider client cleanly.\n\nDone means: Tokenized `--mcp-port` rejects unauthenticated loopback connections, and a scripted fake ACP stdio test agent completes a multi-step tool turn through the panel backend trait without network access.\n\nPart of #1773\n",
